"The XTimers Pro app keeps the underlying activity log on your device. It\n      is not continuously uploaded or synced\n      to your other devices; only a user-requested report sends its displayed\n      application names and derived hostnames. While tracking runs, raw events\n      older than 365 days are removed. Turning tracking off in XTimers stops app\n      recording and removes the app's native-host integration, but does not erase\n      existing history and does not by itself disable an installed browser\n      extension's listeners or active-tab queries. You can clear the log at any\n      time in the app (Automatic Activity Tracking → Reset tracked data).\n      Removing only the app bundle may leave its container or Application Support\n      data, so reset tracked data before removal if you want the locally stored\n      activity erased." = "The XTimers Pro app keeps the underlying activity log on your device. It\n      is not continuously uploaded or synced\n      to your other devices; only a user-requested report sends its displayed\n      application names and derived hostnames. While tracking runs, raw events\n      older than 365 days are removed. Turning tracking off in XTimers stops app\n      recording and removes the app's native-host integration, but does not erase\n      existing history and does not by itself disable an installed browser\n      extension's listeners or active-tab queries. You can clear the log at any\n      time in the app (Automatic Activity Tracking → Reset tracked data).\n      Removing only the app bundle may leave its container or Application Support\n      data, so reset tracked data before removal if you want the locally stored\n      activity erased.";
"The active-tab report is delivered only to the XTimers Pro app running on your own computer — either through the app's local native-messaging host or a loopback (%1$@) connection to the app on the same machine. The extension itself has no remote host and does not transmit the active-tab report over the internet. If the user later asks XTimers Pro to email or publish an activity report, the selected report's application names and derived website hostnames may be sent to XTimers' service for that requested action; raw web addresses and titles are not included, as explained in the %2$@main Privacy Policy%3$@." = "The active-tab report is delivered only to the XTimers Pro app running on your own computer — either through the app's local native-messaging host or a loopback (%1$@) connection to the app on the same machine. The extension itself has no remote host and does not transmit the active-tab report over the internet. If the user later asks XTimers Pro to email or publish an activity report, the selected report's application names and derived website hostnames may be sent to XTimers' service for that requested action; raw web addresses and titles are not included, as explained in the %2$@main Privacy Policy%3$@.";
"The extension inspects the web address and title of the active tab in the\n      most recently focused supported browser. This extension-side query may\n      occur even when another Mac app is currently frontmost. The extension does\n      not read, store, or modify the content of a web page; does not inspect\n      background tabs; does not keep a browsing history of its own; and does not\n      request account identity, credentials, form data, or extension analytics.\n      A web address or title can itself contain information chosen by the site\n      or user. There are no ads and no third-party trackers in the extension." = "The extension inspects the web address and title of the active tab in the\n      most recently focused supported browser. This extension-side query may\n      occur even when another Mac app is currently frontmost. The extension does\n      not read, store, or modify the content of a web page; does not inspect\n      background tabs; does not keep a browsing history of its own; and does not\n      request account identity, credentials, form data, or extension analytics.\n      A web address or title can itself contain information chosen by the site\n      or user. There are no ads and no third-party trackers in the extension.";
"The extension is not directed at children. Its active-tab behavior and\n      controls are the same for every user." = "The extension is not directed at children. Its active-tab behavior and\n      controls are the same for every user.";
